  "text": "87. Which of the following propositions is INCORRECT as regards negligence in civil law\nand in criminal law:\n(A) The jurisprudential concept of negligence differs in civil law and criminal law.\n(B) What may be negligence in civil law may not necessarily be negligence in criminal\nlaw.\n(C) For an act to amount to criminal negligence, the degree of negligence should be\nmuch higher, 1.e. gross or of a very high degree.\n(D) For negligence to amount to both a ‘tort’ and an ‘offence’, the element of mens rea\nmust necessarily be shown to have existed.\nPG 2026 36\np",
